<title>PHILIPPINES: PILTEL FALLS 6.25 PCT ON LOW H1 NET.</title>
<headline>PILTEL FALLS 6.25 PCT ON LOW H1 NET.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pilipino Telephone Corp shares tumbled 75 centavos, or 6.25 percent, to 11.25 pesos in early Monday trade as the market reacted to its low first half earnings, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;People saw that first half earnings were sharply lower,&quot; said Elline Salvatierra, analyst at Anscor-Hagedorn Securities.</p>
<p>The cellular phone company reported late Friday that its first half net income fell to 165.8 million pesos from 487.6 million a year ago.</p>
<p>The company has set aside millions of pesos for its doubtful accounts arising from fraud calls last year.</p>
